### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@roomId = 1
@sessionId = 1

### Create a planned monitoring session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": {{roomId}},
  "name": "Cooling system test",
  "description": "Observe temperature before and after restarting cooling"
}

### List sessions, optionally filtered by room and status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions?roomId={{roomId}}&status=ACTIVE

### Get one session
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions/{{sessionId}}

### Start a planned session
# A room can have only one ACTIVE session.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions/{{sessionId}}/start

### Complete an active session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions/{{sessionId}}/complete

### Cancel a planned or active session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions/{{sessionId}}/cancel

### Add an event to an active session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions/{{sessionId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category": "INTERVENTION",
  "title": "Restarted cooling unit",
  "description": "Airflow returned after the restart",
  "occurredAt": "2026-08-25T10:15:00"
}

### List session events in chronological order
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions/{{sessionId}}/events

### Get the session timeline (readings, events and overlapping alerts)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions/{{sessionId}}/timeline

### Get the timeline for one sensor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions/{{sessionId}}/timeline?sensorId=1

### Export the session as ZIP (15 minutes before and after)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/monitoring-sessions/{{sessionId}}/export

# Event categories: OBSERVATION, INTERVENTION, CONFIGURATION_CHANGE,
# MAINTENANCE, INCIDENT, OTHER. New events are accepted only while the session
# is ACTIVE and their occurredAt must be between startedAt and the current time.
# Timeline readings are bounded and downsampled to at most 200 displayed points
# per sensor. `readingsTruncated` indicates that only the latest 5,000 source
# readings were considered.
# The ZIP export contains session.csv, readings.csv, events.csv, and alerts.csv.
# Full readings use the configured export row limit and include a session_phase.
